# Translating Loki Setup

After configuring the build, run `make update-po` with GNU gettext installed.
This extracts C and Glade strings into `po/setup.pot` and
`po/loki-uninstall.pot` and merges changes into the locale catalogs.

Edit `po/<locale>/setup.po` for the installer and `po/<locale>/loki-uninstall.po`
for the uninstaller and Check and Rescue. Use UTF-8, preserve format placeholders
and review entries marked `fuzzy`. Remove that flag after verifying the
translation. Untranslated and fuzzy messages display in English.

Run `make gettext` to validate and compile the catalogs in
`image/setup.data/locale/`. Commit the updated catalogs with their `.mo` files
so packaged installers use the current translations.

To add a locale, add its name to `LOCALES` in `Makefile.in`, create
`po/<locale>/`, and use `msginit --locale=<locale> --input=po/<domain>.pot
--output-file=po/<locale>/<domain>.po` for each domain.
